1
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:51,940
[Mystic Nine]
[Adapted from the novel of Kennedy Xu]

2
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,980
[Episode 13]
[This story is purely fictional]

3
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:12,660
See that?

4
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,100
There's a place down there

5
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:15,820
we very much want to enter.

6
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,980
But nothing we've tried has worked.

7
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:21,450
There is, however, one kind of animal

8
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:22,980
that can get inside.

9
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,980
It's extremely difficult to catch.

10
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:28,980
We went to great lengths to capture one.

11
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,890
It's very clever.

12
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:33,170
It has a fair degree of intelligence

13
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,850
and can even be trained.

14
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:38,130
What is it?

15
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,170
You'll find out soon enough.

16
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,220
Unit 401?

17
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:25,260
If you can complete this task,

18
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:27,340
I'll explain the scientific principles

19
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:27,890
behind the Otherworld Tower.

20
00:03:28,470 --> 00:03:30,730
The secrets I know and the place I'm headed

21
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:32,170
are far beyond anything in the Otherworld Tower.

22
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:21,730
You know,

23
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,050
capturing it cost

24
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:25,340
the lives of over 100

25
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,810
of our Japanese comrades.

26
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,220
Our lighting equipment was inadequate then.

27
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:32,980
We couldn't see it in the dark

28
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:36,900
and had to feel our way around to catch it.

29
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,290
Whatever you need,

30
00:05:43,870 --> 00:05:44,730
ask Mr. Tanaka.

31
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:47,660
He'll equip you immediately.

32
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,250
But if you fail to tame it,

33
00:05:51,630 --> 00:05:53,050
please don't come out again.

34
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,810
If I manage to tame it,

35
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,140
will you let me leave?

36
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:03,610
We Japanese are true to our word.

37
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,700
The mighty Empire of Japan

38
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,850
has nothing to fear from a nobody like you.

39
00:06:11,270 --> 00:06:12,700
Tame it successfully,

40
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,170
and I'll let you leave.

41
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:25,250
Fine.

42
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:28,580
I'll tame it.

43
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:30,980
I look forward to your results.

44
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:33,340
One more thing.

45
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,900
Be sure to remember:

46
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:38,020
when you sleep at night,

47
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,290
stay well away from it.

48
00:07:55,390 --> 00:07:56,370
How much farther?

49
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,810
About another li, I'd say.

50
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:02,930
You're not playing me, are you?

51
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:13,100
There's something I haven't told you.

52
00:08:15,160 --> 00:08:15,810
What is it?

53
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,810
I was the Otherworld Patriarch.

54
00:08:27,870 --> 00:08:28,810
I was one of his followers.

55
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:32,610
You've met him?

56
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:33,890
No.

57
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,580
After I was crippled, someone duped me into joining his sect.

58
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:41,060
What did you do after joining?

59
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:42,300
I built walls.

60
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,940
I've seen that high wall you mentioned.

61
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,770
How much do you know about the tower?

62
00:08:56,630 --> 00:08:58,010
Nothing, really.

63
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,980
I left after only a couple of days.

64
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:03,220
I'd realized

65
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,980
something terrible must have happened inside.

66
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:10,490
That was why they were walling off the entire tower.

67
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:11,460
Of course,

68
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:13,850
that's also how I learned

69
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:16,130
there was an underground river beneath the Otherworld Tower.

70
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:19,060
So you left before you learned anything

71
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:19,850
about the sect?

72
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:20,940
Why would I stay?

73
00:09:22,030 --> 00:09:22,820
Besides,

74
00:09:23,510 --> 00:09:25,530
if the Otherworld Patriarch were truly that powerful,

75
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:26,820
he should have foreseen

76
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:27,890
something would happen in the tower.

77
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:29,820
He wouldn't have needed us to build walls

78
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,650
and seal the tower off.

79
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:34,940
Nothing gets past you, Third Master. Impressive.

80
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:39,220
My legs may be crippled,

81
00:09:39,910 --> 00:09:40,850
but my mind isn't.

82
00:09:43,270 --> 00:09:43,700
Let's go.

83
00:10:04,390 --> 00:10:04,980
Wait.

84
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:23,340
The leaves on this side have more dew on them.

85
00:10:25,030 --> 00:10:25,580
The air is damper.

86
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:27,460
Go this way.

87
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:40,730
Stop.

88
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:53,180
Light it

89
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:56,220
and watch where the smoke goes.

90
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:25,700
There.

91
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:47,650
I hear water.

92
00:11:48,670 --> 00:11:49,460
The current is swift.

93
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,250
It must be an underground river.

94
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:55,530
Then it should be the one

95
00:11:55,550 --> 00:11:56,420
beneath the Otherworld Tower.

96
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:59,530
But I couldn't say whether the Japanese

97
00:11:59,550 --> 00:12:00,700
passed through here.

98
00:12:02,790 --> 00:12:04,290
The earth is loose and the rocks unstable.

99
00:12:04,670 --> 00:12:05,610
If we blast through,

100
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:07,580
it could easily collapse.

101
00:12:09,910 --> 00:12:11,460
You brought me here for a reason, Third Master.

102
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,860
You must have a way.

103
00:12:18,670 --> 00:12:19,460
Down there,

104
00:12:20,270 --> 00:12:21,300
the current isn't the only danger.

105
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,010
There are hidden rocks everywhere.

106
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,850
I've been reading the terrain all along

107
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,370
and found that the underground river

108
00:12:27,670 --> 00:12:29,850
has a raised ridge here, like a dragon's spine.

109
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,770
That means

110
00:12:32,390 --> 00:12:35,180
there must be a natural stone dam below.

111
00:12:35,870 --> 00:12:37,180
You haven't even gone down there,

112
00:12:38,150 --> 00:12:40,250
yet you already know what lies in the river.

113
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:41,940
You truly are an old hand.

114
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:44,220
Isn't it obvious?

115
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,650
Look at the terrain.

116
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,180
A descending ridge crosses a watercourse here.

117
00:12:49,550 --> 00:12:51,610
Where they cross, there must be a stone dam.

118
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:55,220
Anything carried down from the upper reaches

119
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,460
will get stuck at that very spot.

120
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,610
This magnetic snare

121
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:04,890
is an old gold prospector's device.

122
00:13:05,270 --> 00:13:08,100
Lower it through this crack.

123
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,850
If the Japanese dropped

124
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,700
anything made of iron upstream,

125
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,180
the magnet will draw it up.

126
00:13:14,870 --> 00:13:17,420
Of course, whether this works

127
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,420
depends on your skill and luck, Master Zhang.

128
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:22,370
This is your specialty, Third Master.

129
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:24,460
I wouldn't presume to show off before you.

130
00:13:25,790 --> 00:13:26,370
No.

131
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,530
My gout has been acting up.

132
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,060
My wrist hurts badly.

133
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,010
You do it.

134
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:42,610
Master Zhang,

135
00:14:43,030 --> 00:14:45,820
you've clearly never seen how a starving beggar

136
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:48,180
picks grains of rice from a pavement crack.

137
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:52,300
Brute force won't work.

138
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:56,220
You have to do it like this.

139
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,580
Brace your little finger against the edge.

140
00:15:00,930 --> 00:15:02,850
Keep your index and middle fingers three hao apart.

141
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:04,610
Feel the speed of the current.

142
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:05,580
Wait for the right moment,

143
00:15:05,750 --> 00:15:07,250
then flick your wrist

144
00:15:08,270 --> 00:15:09,250
like this.

145
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,250
Too hard,

146
00:15:12,270 --> 00:15:13,420
and you crush the grain.

147
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:15,010
Too light,

148
00:15:16,030 --> 00:15:17,420
and you come up empty-handed.

149
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:20,270
Back when I lived on the streets of Changsha,

150
00:15:20,270 --> 00:15:22,010
this very trick

151
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:24,490
kept me alive in the gutters for three years.

152
00:15:25,270 --> 00:15:26,060
But no matter.

153
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:29,180
We've got

154
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,060
plenty of time

155
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:32,580
and magnets.

156
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:35,300
Keep practicing.

157
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:45,650
It may be a beggar's trick,

158
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:47,770
but it can save your life when it counts.

159
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,610
A Far East Conquest Medal.

160
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,650
The Japanese did use this route.

161
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:45,100
In that case,

162
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:47,770
my men will find out

163
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:50,530
where this river leads.

164
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:57,860
[Baihua Benevolence Hall]

165
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,220
You're here.

166
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:23,180
Why didn't you let me know you were back?

167
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:32,490
I hear the Mystic Nine even held a meeting.

168
00:17:33,750 --> 00:17:35,220
How did it go?

169
00:17:35,550 --> 00:17:37,770
Have you been working for the Japanese all along?

170
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:42,050
You underestimate me.

171
00:17:43,550 --> 00:17:47,660
I've always looked out only for myself.

172
00:17:49,270 --> 00:17:51,660
Did you leave marks down there?

173
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:18,330
Impressive, Miss Huo.

174
00:18:22,550 --> 00:18:25,010
You actually found it.

175
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:27,330
Now I won't have to go down myself.

176
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,570
So this really is what you wanted.

177
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:31,940
What exactly is it?

178
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:34,460
You brought it out yourself,

179
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,290
yet you don't know what it is?

180
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:47,250
Sand?

181
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,220
I don't know.

182
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:54,140
Did you see

183
00:18:54,830 --> 00:18:57,140
magic inside the Otherworld Tower?

184
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,730
This

185
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,180
is the secret behind it.

186
00:19:05,750 --> 00:19:06,810
With this,

187
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:11,220
I have nothing to fear from Zhang Qishan.

188
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:15,810
It's time you kept

189
00:19:17,270 --> 00:19:18,220
your promise.

190
00:19:22,550 --> 00:19:23,490
These

191
00:19:23,830 --> 00:19:25,490
are the Huo Clan's IOUs.

192
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:30,460
[Debt Acknowledgment]
Your clan's debt to me is wiped clean.

193
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:38,460
But while the financial debt is settled,

194
00:19:39,270 --> 00:19:40,700
you and I have now

195
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:43,460
incurred another debt by colluding with the Japanese.

196
00:19:47,030 --> 00:19:50,180
It may seem you can part ways with me,

197
00:19:50,370 --> 00:19:54,860
but in truth, we're bound more tightly than ever.

198
00:19:58,830 --> 00:20:00,530
The Huo Clan isn't afraid to take you down with us.

199
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:02,940
It needn't come to that.

200
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:07,900
Working with the Japanese doesn't always end badly.

201
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,050
Don't worry.

202
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,660
I guarantee that if you do your utmost,

203
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:14,250
the Huo Clan will survive.

204
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:15,660
Of course,

205
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:18,050
only the Huo Clan will.

206
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:20,530
What are you going to do to the Mystic Nine?

207
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:25,380
Master Qiansui.

208
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:28,940
No need to leave.

209
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:31,570
Xiangu and I are in the same boat.

210
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,810
She's already in too deep.

211
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,460
Isn't that right, Xiangu?

212
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:39,090
Master Qiansui,

213
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:41,330
our men have caught up with Qi Tiezui.

214
00:20:41,550 --> 00:20:42,250
We can strike at any time.

215
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:45,180
Then kill him.

216
00:20:45,590 --> 00:20:46,980
Don't hesitate.

217
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:47,900
Yes.

218
00:20:52,070 --> 00:20:52,730
Ding Qiansui...

219
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:54,620
There's no need to be so surprised.

220
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:57,220
Tiezui is only the first.

221
00:20:58,310 --> 00:21:00,700
The second will follow soon.

222
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,180
Then the third.

223
00:21:04,110 --> 00:21:04,860
Xiangu,

224
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,810
if you tell anyone,

225
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,770
what you and I have done will come to light.

226
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,490
You'll have no place

227
00:21:12,590 --> 00:21:16,250
in the Mystic Nine or in Changsha.

228
00:21:16,920 --> 00:21:19,220
How about this?

229
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:23,460
Let's devise a grand plan today.

230
00:21:25,310 --> 00:21:26,460
Once Tiezui is dead,

231
00:21:27,750 --> 00:21:29,860
Zhang Qishan will be furious.

232
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,660
You and I will both be in danger.

233
00:21:36,550 --> 00:21:37,980
But don't worry.

234
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:42,900
I always keep something in reserve.

235
00:21:43,310 --> 00:21:45,460
I learned that in the palace.

236
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:49,900
With this treasure

237
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,140
you brought me,

238
00:21:51,550 --> 00:21:53,420
Yoshiyuki Hatoyama and I

239
00:21:55,350 --> 00:21:58,530
will be Zhang Qishan's undoing.

240
00:22:01,700 --> 00:22:04,480
[Ding Qiansui's personal information]

241
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:04,980
Master Zhang,

242
00:22:05,510 --> 00:22:07,660
Xiaojin has uncovered Ding Qiansui's entire background.

243
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:08,980
He is no ordinary man.

244
00:22:09,790 --> 00:22:10,730
He has changed his citizenship.

245
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:11,900
Legally speaking,

246
00:22:12,310 --> 00:22:13,530
he's now an American.

247
00:22:15,480 --> 00:22:16,250
Tell me everything.

248
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,380
Ding Qiansui,

249
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:19,010
formerly Ding Shichang, was a native of Changsha.

250
00:22:19,590 --> 00:22:20,860
He became a eunuch at the palace at eight,

251
00:22:21,240 --> 00:22:22,220
serving in the Imperial Kitchen.

252
00:22:23,110 --> 00:22:24,090
During the Guangxu reign,

253
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:25,490
there was a Belgian missionary in the palace

254
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:26,730
named Joseph Vanderburg.

255
00:22:27,510 --> 00:22:28,700
He supplied Empress Dowager Cixi

256
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:29,980
with Western pastries.

257
00:22:30,830 --> 00:22:31,420
Ding Qiansui

258
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:32,860
went to great lengths to ingratiate himself with him.

259
00:22:33,110 --> 00:22:34,050
Through that connection,

260
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:35,660
he secured work procuring supplies outside the palace.

261
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:36,730
At 13,

262
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:37,860
Ding Qiansui

263
00:22:38,030 --> 00:22:39,770
followed Joseph Vanderburg to Shanghai.

264
00:22:40,310 --> 00:22:41,730
He first sought the protection of the Belgians

265
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:43,180
at a church in the French Concession.

266
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:46,050
Soon afterward, he made contact with the Southern Presbyterian Church

267
00:22:46,720 --> 00:22:48,140
and wormed his way into a post at Guangci Hospital.

268
00:22:48,400 --> 00:22:49,140
That same year,

269
00:22:49,720 --> 00:22:51,850
he was baptized, took the Christian name Samuel Ding,

270
00:22:52,480 --> 00:22:54,050
and formally began studying theology.

271
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,170
Then, under a special provision for church members,

272
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:58,570
he applied for special registration

273
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:01,140
and formally became a US citizen at 16.

274
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:03,380
When he returned to the palace with that status,

275
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:04,490
he became even more influential.

276
00:23:05,110 --> 00:23:07,010
Everyone had to show him respect.

277
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:13,090
A palace eunuch

278
00:23:14,350 --> 00:23:15,220
transformed himself

279
00:23:16,350 --> 00:23:17,570
into an American citizen.

280
00:23:19,830 --> 00:23:21,420
No ordinary man could have pulled that off.

281
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:24,220
When the Qing dynasty fell,

282
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:26,180
he immediately fled with palace silver

283
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,010
and turned to the Americans.

284
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:28,140
At 42,

285
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:29,380
the Americans arranged for him

286
00:23:29,640 --> 00:23:30,460
to come to Changsha.

287
00:23:31,070 --> 00:23:32,980
On the surface, he ran a foreign trading firm,

288
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,460
but in secret,

289
00:23:35,110 --> 00:23:37,010
he laundered money for the Americans.

290
00:23:38,510 --> 00:23:39,730
But the Americans didn't trust him either.

291
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:42,570
They kept him away from important business.

292
00:23:43,110 --> 00:23:44,700
Unable to profit from it,

293
00:23:45,880 --> 00:23:46,330
he had no choice

294
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,810
but to secretly court the Japanese.

295
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,420
The Stars and Stripes in one hand,

296
00:23:56,750 --> 00:23:57,900
the Japanese flag in the other.

297
00:23:58,830 --> 00:23:59,660
If we move against him,

298
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:02,860
we may provoke both consulates.

299
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:04,290
Master Zhang,

300
00:24:04,830 --> 00:24:05,660
there's one more thing.

301
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:07,770
He's no longer at Taihe House.

302
00:24:08,640 --> 00:24:09,530
Once we left the Otherworld Tower,

303
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:11,380
he moved into Baihua Benevolence Hall.

304
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:13,220
Since then,

305
00:24:14,680 --> 00:24:15,770
he hasn't shown his face.

306
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:20,260
[Ding Shichang, Application for U.S. Citizenship]

307
00:24:23,590 --> 00:24:25,330
Ding Qiansui must have realized

308
00:24:25,830 --> 00:24:27,730
we'd uncovered his ties to the Japanese,

309
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,570
so he went into hiding.

310
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:31,860
To get to him now,

311
00:24:31,880 --> 00:24:33,220
we'd have to storm the consulate.

312
00:24:33,750 --> 00:24:34,810
Once it causes an uproar,

313
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,810
the American Consulate

314
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,460
will undoubtedly intervene.

315
00:24:39,030 --> 00:24:39,980
Then this matter

316
00:24:40,640 --> 00:24:42,250
will become a diplomatic incident.

317
00:24:43,590 --> 00:24:45,010
That's why I came to you.

318
00:24:47,790 --> 00:24:48,730
You came to me

319
00:24:49,310 --> 00:24:50,420
not for my wits,

320
00:24:51,350 --> 00:24:53,090
but because you're desperate to save Wu Laogou, right?

321
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:58,250
Has your opinion of Wu Laogou changed?

322
00:25:04,510 --> 00:25:05,770
Why don't you tell me first

323
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:07,980
what kind of man

324
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:09,460
you think he is now?

325
00:25:09,830 --> 00:25:11,570
How has your view of him changed?

326
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:15,770
I want to live.

327
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,010
I want food on the table

328
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:19,420
and the chance to live with dignity.

329
00:25:20,830 --> 00:25:21,860
I'll trust you one more time.

330
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:24,340
You'd better catch it.

331
00:25:25,270 --> 00:25:27,290
I believe there's a one-in-ten chance you'll protect the Mystic Nine.

332
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:29,090
I'll bet on that chance.

333
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:32,730
I'll help you.

334
00:25:34,070 --> 00:25:34,810
He's brave and resourceful,

335
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:36,810
with a pure heart,

336
00:25:40,510 --> 00:25:42,900
though he's not well-educated.

337
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,010
Given your usual temperament,

338
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,380
you'd never be so reckless

339
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:51,420
as to move against Ding Qiansui like this.

340
00:25:51,830 --> 00:25:53,250
You've come to agree with me.

341
00:25:54,160 --> 00:25:55,570
Laogou is vital to the Mystic Nine.

342
00:25:58,590 --> 00:25:59,660
He is indeed.

343
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,090
So,

344
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:07,530
difficult as this may be,

345
00:26:08,270 --> 00:26:09,420
it isn't impossible.

346
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,660
First, we need to make them think

347
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:14,220
Ding Qiansui is a spent pawn,

348
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:17,810
but one that still has some use.

349
00:26:18,350 --> 00:26:19,810
Ninth Master, what should we do?

350
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,770
Thirty years ago, smallpox ravaged Beiping.

351
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:25,460
Bodies lay piled at the ends of alleys,

352
00:26:25,510 --> 00:26:26,700
uncollected for days.

353
00:26:27,750 --> 00:26:29,730
Though cowpox inoculation is now available,

354
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,010
the disease hasn't been eradicated.

355
00:26:32,070 --> 00:26:33,330
Once the disease breaks out,

356
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:34,090
everyone will panic.

357
00:26:35,510 --> 00:26:36,940
The church won't keep him there.

358
00:26:37,200 --> 00:26:39,900
They'll send him to a hospital at once.

359
00:26:40,960 --> 00:26:41,900
As far as I know,

360
00:26:42,590 --> 00:26:44,660
the church has its own hospital in Changsha.

361
00:26:45,070 --> 00:26:45,620
Yes,

362
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,490
but more than one.

363
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:50,330
St. Marie Hospital

364
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:51,180
is run by foreigners.

365
00:26:51,830 --> 00:26:53,330
Puji Hospital, on the other hand,

366
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,770
is nominally affiliated with the church,

367
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,570
but is actually run by the local authorities.

368
00:26:58,200 --> 00:27:00,380
As long as Ding Qiansui is sent to Puji,

369
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:02,570
once he's beyond the church's protection,

370
00:27:04,400 --> 00:27:05,900
he'll be in our hands.

371
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:11,700
Giving Ding Qiansui real smallpox won't be easy,

372
00:27:13,070 --> 00:27:13,700
but...

373
00:27:27,830 --> 00:27:31,620
What has Zhang Qishan been up to?

374
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:33,420
He's sent several groups of men

375
00:27:33,440 --> 00:27:34,290
to scout your residence.

376
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:36,700
I hear he even checked your household registration.

377
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:41,940
He must have been shocked

378
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:44,180
to learn I'm an American citizen.

379
00:27:45,030 --> 00:27:47,380
Now, even if he wants to move against me,

380
00:27:48,070 --> 00:27:49,730
there's nothing he can do.

381
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:57,220
I'd love to see that defeated look on his face.

382
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:00,920
The paper is coated

383
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:02,570
- with musk and aconite ointment.
- Putting up a blessing!

384
00:28:03,030 --> 00:28:04,420
It smells like rice paste.

385
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:05,350
- A blessing! - Go away!

386
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:06,540
- Once it touches the skin... - Go away!

387
00:28:06,540 --> 00:28:08,330
- The medicine will slowly seep in.
- Whose child is this?

388
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:11,140
- Within three to five days...
- Go!

389
00:28:11,680 --> 00:28:12,740
- Blisters and swelling will appear...
- I'm sorry.

390
00:28:13,080 --> 00:28:14,530
Looking almost identical to smallpox.

391
00:28:14,550 --> 00:28:16,460
You let just anyone come near me?

392
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:20,050
Had that been one of Zhang Qishan's men,

393
00:28:20,790 --> 00:28:22,620
wouldn't I already be dead?

394
00:28:23,480 --> 00:28:24,940
Keep your eyes open,

395
00:28:25,510 --> 00:28:26,420
you useless servant.

396
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:27,980
Yes, Master.

397
00:28:29,310 --> 00:28:30,330
Day one.

398
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:34,290
Next, Master Zhang, you need only send men

399
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:36,220
to spread a rumor near the church

400
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:39,900
that someone has returned from a smallpox-stricken area.

401
00:28:40,350 --> 00:28:41,250
Within days,

402
00:28:41,590 --> 00:28:43,490
panic will sweep through Changsha.

403
00:28:43,830 --> 00:28:45,940
By then, whether Ding Qiansui is truly infected

404
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,220
will no longer matter.

405
00:28:47,510 --> 00:28:48,770
The Americans certainly won't let him

406
00:28:48,830 --> 00:28:49,900
remain in the church.

407
00:28:50,110 --> 00:28:50,660
Exactly.

408
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:52,490
But there is still one problem:

409
00:28:53,070 --> 00:28:54,420
how do we get them to sign

410
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:57,140
and send Ding Qiansui to Puji Hospital?

411
00:28:57,160 --> 00:28:59,330
I'll take care of that.

412
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:22,090
That's...

413
00:29:22,920 --> 00:29:23,570
smallpox!

414
00:29:24,270 --> 00:29:25,250
It's smallpox!

415
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:26,460
This man has smallpox!

416
00:29:26,750 --> 00:29:27,620
Everyone, run!

417
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:28,290
Run!

418
00:29:28,640 --> 00:29:29,460
Run!

419
00:29:29,920 --> 00:29:30,940
Get out of here!

420
00:29:35,070 --> 00:29:36,090
I'm telling you,

421
00:29:36,550 --> 00:29:38,140
I'm an American!

422
00:29:38,830 --> 00:29:40,220
Who says I have smallpox?

423
00:29:40,510 --> 00:29:41,700
You set me up!

424
00:29:43,270 --> 00:29:44,140
Who are you?

425
00:29:44,140 --> 00:29:45,100
[Triage Form]

426
00:29:45,960 --> 00:29:46,460
Take him away.

427
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:50,220
Let go of me!

428
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:20,700
Zhang Qishan,

429
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:23,900
you've set up a private prison

430
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:26,660
and detained an American citizen.

431
00:30:28,310 --> 00:30:30,050
That's a capital offense!

432
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:33,140
Let me out!

433
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:36,770
Let me out!

434
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:40,180
Shout as loudly as you like.

435
00:30:41,790 --> 00:30:43,050
No one will ever know you're here.

436
00:30:48,720 --> 00:30:50,380
What is your connection to Yoshiyuki Hatoyama?

437
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:52,140
What is he doing in the Otherworld Tower?

438
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:53,250
Why did he capture Wu Laogou?

439
00:30:53,350 --> 00:30:54,770
Where are they now? Speak!

440
00:31:00,640 --> 00:31:01,900
Zhang Qishan,

441
00:31:03,240 --> 00:31:05,700
don't think you can frighten me.

442
00:31:06,680 --> 00:31:11,180
I've seen every filthy trick the palace had to offer.

443
00:31:11,510 --> 00:31:12,940
I'm an old man.

444
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:15,530
I can't withstand much.

445
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:17,460
If I die,

446
00:31:18,350 --> 00:31:20,980
the Americans will come after you.

447
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:34,900
Back home, we have a special torture technique.

448
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:36,940
With it, I can crush

449
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:39,490
your skull with one hand.

450
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:46,940
Once the skull begins to crack,

451
00:31:49,030 --> 00:31:51,250
no matter how strong your will,

452
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:55,180
you won't be able to endure the pain.

453
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:58,980
From this moment on,

454
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:01,770
you'll feel as though your skull

455
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,900
is clamped in a giant iron vise.

456
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:06,570
Your head

457
00:32:07,110 --> 00:32:09,530
will feel like a balloon being pumped full,

458
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:12,860
swelling from the inside out.

459
00:32:14,790 --> 00:32:15,860
Then

460
00:32:16,510 --> 00:32:17,660
you'll hear

461
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:21,050
a series of popping sounds.

462
00:32:22,720 --> 00:32:24,330
Those are your blood vessels

463
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:26,180
bursting one by one.

464
00:32:45,790 --> 00:32:49,420
Zhang... Zhang Qishan, you're insane!

465
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,420
You think I'm afraid?

466
00:32:59,270 --> 00:33:00,860
I'll talk!

467
00:33:01,830 --> 00:33:04,420
I'll tell you everything!

468
00:33:16,480 --> 00:33:17,380
I never

469
00:33:18,550 --> 00:33:21,010
wanted dealings with the Japanese.

470
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:24,570
Back then, they claimed to support the Qing,

471
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:27,980
waving the banner of loyalty to the emperor.

472
00:33:28,550 --> 00:33:29,420
And what happened?

473
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:33,250
They forced the court to cede land and pay indemnities.

474
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:36,090
Such treacherous people...

475
00:33:36,680 --> 00:33:40,660
How could I ever trust them?

476
00:33:41,550 --> 00:33:43,250
How did you make contact?

477
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:44,490
Tottori,

478
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:48,570
Yoshiyuki Hatoyama's superior.

479
00:33:49,070 --> 00:33:50,700
Torii Totori

480
00:33:51,030 --> 00:33:52,730
came to me himself.

481
00:33:52,760 --> 00:33:54,380
Beneath Changsha, there is a secret place

482
00:33:54,550 --> 00:33:55,530
of immense importance.

483
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,490
My men are trapped there.

484
00:33:58,310 --> 00:34:00,120
Zhang Qishan, who leads the Mystic Nine,

485
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,310
killed all our agents.

486
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:05,180
I need a Chinese contact above ground.

487
00:34:06,310 --> 00:34:08,050
I'm an American.

488
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,090
Why should I help you?

489
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:13,860
An American?

490
00:34:17,960 --> 00:34:19,980
The Americans want nothing from China

491
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,130
but its markets and the profits

492
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:23,090
they can extract.

493
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:25,340
Stay with them,

494
00:34:27,110 --> 00:34:28,610
and you'll only scrape by,

495
00:34:28,710 --> 00:34:30,090
never able to truly rise in the world.

496
00:34:31,030 --> 00:34:32,690
But the Empire of Japan

497
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:34,940
wants this land itself.

498
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:38,460
Sooner or later, it will all be ours.

499
00:34:41,510 --> 00:34:43,010
Help me now,

500
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:45,650
and one day you'll stand above the rest.

501
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:47,460
Otherwise,

502
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,980
once the dust settles,

503
00:34:49,550 --> 00:34:52,300
you'll still be a servant begging on your knees.

504
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:54,050
I'm

505
00:34:56,760 --> 00:34:58,260
not a whole man.

506
00:34:59,320 --> 00:35:00,300
I'd had enough

507
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:04,010
of being a servant.

508
00:35:05,160 --> 00:35:06,530
To rise above my station,

509
00:35:07,710 --> 00:35:10,300
a foreign passport alone would never

510
00:35:11,550 --> 00:35:12,340
be enough.

511
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:18,010
I had to become a true master.

512
00:35:18,010 --> 00:35:19,670
[Taihe Pleasure House]

513
00:35:19,670 --> 00:35:21,860
With the help of the Japanese,

514
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:24,090
I bought Taihe House

515
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:26,690
to supply Hatoyama with provisions.

516
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:41,650
There really were people beneath Changsha.

517
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,130
Remarkable.

518
00:35:44,400 --> 00:35:45,650
I later learned

519
00:35:46,070 --> 00:35:47,780
his name was Yoshiyuki Hatoyama.

520
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:01,690
What else did Hatoyama

521
00:36:02,320 --> 00:36:03,650
tell you about the Otherworld Tower?

522
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:05,740
He spoke little,

523
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:08,420
explained nothing,

524
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:10,420
and only gave orders.

525
00:36:12,590 --> 00:36:14,420
I simply obeyed.

526
00:36:14,710 --> 00:36:15,860
Actually,

527
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:19,420
you needn't concern yourselves too much with that tower.

528
00:36:19,710 --> 00:36:23,530
It's merely a decoy.

529
00:36:24,360 --> 00:36:26,690
Hatoyama's true destination

530
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:29,570
is never the Otherworld Tower.

531
00:36:31,920 --> 00:36:33,740
It's the end of the underground river.

532
00:36:34,150 --> 00:36:35,900
You know about the underground river?

533
00:36:36,150 --> 00:36:37,780
How did you find out?

534
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:39,610
Where does it end? Tell me.

535
00:36:41,150 --> 00:36:42,050
Xiangxi.

536
00:36:42,800 --> 00:36:47,130
I only know it's somewhere in Xiangxi.

537
00:36:47,590 --> 00:36:49,130
Everything they did

538
00:36:49,510 --> 00:36:51,610
was to reach that place.

539
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,010
What's in Xiangxi?

540
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,300
Does it have something to do with the Otherworld Patriarch

541
00:36:55,710 --> 00:36:56,740
or Yin Changsheng?

542
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:57,940
What is Hatoyama really after?

543
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,860
I don't know.

544
00:37:00,630 --> 00:37:03,420
I just worked all that out myself.

545
00:37:05,590 --> 00:37:06,900
I'm no fool.

546
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,170
What about Unit 401?

547
00:37:17,070 --> 00:37:19,860
Hatoyama arranged that too.

548
00:37:20,670 --> 00:37:22,860
He gave me some pills

549
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:27,170
that make people obey.

550
00:37:28,590 --> 00:37:29,340
Go on.

551
00:37:30,280 --> 00:37:32,260
I believe it was magic.

552
00:37:33,070 --> 00:37:34,530
And he mastered it,

553
00:37:35,550 --> 00:37:36,570
gaining divine powers

554
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:39,740
to read fate and glimpse Heaven's secrets.

555
00:37:41,630 --> 00:37:44,090
Perhaps he can hear

556
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:45,980
this very conversation

557
00:37:47,110 --> 00:37:49,170
right now.

558
00:37:57,640 --> 00:37:58,460
You must know

559
00:37:59,720 --> 00:38:00,860
more than that.

560
00:38:01,110 --> 00:38:04,940
After working with Yoshiyuki Hatoyama all these years,

561
00:38:05,560 --> 00:38:07,100
I discovered long ago

562
00:38:07,830 --> 00:38:10,570
the secret behind the tower's magic.

563
00:38:11,150 --> 00:38:14,220
Yet he always said it wasn't magic

564
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:15,850
but science.

565
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:17,690
What nonsense.

566
00:38:19,590 --> 00:38:20,610
How does the magic work?

567
00:38:21,110 --> 00:38:23,780
Tell me, and you may yet redeem yourself.

568
00:38:27,510 --> 00:38:28,940
Zhang Qishan,

569
00:38:30,510 --> 00:38:33,300
you think far too highly of yourself.

570
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:38,340
Since I know how the magic works,

571
00:38:40,960 --> 00:38:46,170
I can reverse time itself!

572
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:20,210
I'm leaving.

573
00:39:22,110 --> 00:39:23,690
Zhang Qishan,

574
00:39:25,550 --> 00:39:26,570
farewell.

575
00:40:13,710 --> 00:40:14,490
Come here.

576
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,340
Sir.

577
00:40:17,440 --> 00:40:18,610
We're past the checkpoint.

578
00:40:19,510 --> 00:40:20,650
Now tell me.

579
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:23,010
Why did you pay to join our caravan?

580
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,980
Well, these are troubled times,

581
00:40:27,510 --> 00:40:28,820
and bandits are everywhere.

582
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:29,820
Traveling with you

583
00:40:30,070 --> 00:40:30,900
is safer.

584
00:40:31,710 --> 00:40:33,090
You expect me to believe

585
00:40:33,510 --> 00:40:34,740
such nonsense?

586
00:40:35,190 --> 00:40:35,780
Get lost.

587
00:40:37,230 --> 00:40:37,690
Sir,

588
00:40:38,710 --> 00:40:39,210
well...

589
00:40:40,760 --> 00:40:41,780
I'll be honest with you.

590
00:40:42,550 --> 00:40:43,260
You just seemed

591
00:40:43,480 --> 00:40:44,900
like a man I could trust.

592
00:40:50,280 --> 00:40:51,490
Times are hard.

593
00:40:52,550 --> 00:40:53,380
But don't worry.

594
00:40:54,110 --> 00:40:55,570
Since I took your money,

595
00:40:56,190 --> 00:40:57,650
I'll keep your secret.

596
00:40:58,480 --> 00:40:59,570
I know Hankou well.

597
00:40:59,670 --> 00:41:00,380
Once we get there,

598
00:41:00,510 --> 00:41:03,090
I'll find you a few good places to hide.

599
00:41:04,030 --> 00:41:05,570
Thank you, sir. Thank you.

600
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:06,420
Sir,

601
00:41:07,110 --> 00:41:09,130
may I ask

602
00:41:09,510 --> 00:41:10,130
one more thing?

603
00:41:10,670 --> 00:41:13,260
Have you ever been to Xishan?

604
00:41:13,880 --> 00:41:16,490
I hear there's an old Daoist temple there.

605
00:41:18,630 --> 00:41:19,530
I'd like to take a look.

606
00:41:19,710 --> 00:41:20,530
What a coincidence.

607
00:41:21,510 --> 00:41:22,900
Whenever we transport goods,

608
00:41:23,150 --> 00:41:25,690
we detour through Xishan to hunt for jars.

609
00:41:25,880 --> 00:41:26,780
Hunt for jars?

610
00:41:27,230 --> 00:41:27,690
That's right.

611
00:41:27,820 --> 00:41:28,960
[Good Fortune]

612
00:41:28,960 --> 00:41:31,260
That temple was built by the Otherworld Immortal.

613
00:41:31,630 --> 00:41:33,460
Legend says he could control time.

614
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:35,420
So his followers devised

615
00:41:35,440 --> 00:41:36,940
a way to store treasures for a century.

616
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:39,570
They sealed fine wine and tea in ritual jars

617
00:41:39,710 --> 00:41:40,820
and buried them at the temple,

618
00:41:40,920 --> 00:41:43,690
then asked the Patriarch to send them a century into the future.

619
00:41:44,230 --> 00:41:46,610
By the time they were unearthed, the wine would've aged for a century,

620
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,260
and the tea would've become highly prized.

621
00:41:48,670 --> 00:41:50,780
That's why we often try our luck there.

622
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:54,260
Sadly, most of what we find is worthless.

623
00:42:37,630 --> 00:42:40,690
More visitors. Greetings, gentlemen.

624
00:42:51,550 --> 00:42:53,780
Quite a crowd hunting for jars today.

625
00:42:54,550 --> 00:42:56,820
My friend, this area is ours.

626
00:42:57,230 --> 00:42:58,210
If you want to hunt,

627
00:42:58,590 --> 00:42:59,210
go over there.

628
00:43:52,840 --> 00:43:53,900
What did Zhang Qishan

629
00:43:54,510 --> 00:43:56,010
send you here to investigate?

630
00:43:58,510 --> 00:44:00,170
Why not tell your own fortune

631
00:44:01,630 --> 00:44:03,010
and see how you'll die?

632
00:44:08,800 --> 00:44:09,490
Will you do it or not?

633
00:44:11,110 --> 00:44:12,900
I will!

634
00:44:30,880 --> 00:44:31,490
Well?

635
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:33,860
How does it say you'll die?

636
00:44:35,800 --> 00:44:36,860
The signs say

637
00:44:38,760 --> 00:44:39,940
I won't die.

638
00:44:41,710 --> 00:44:42,530
Is that so?

639
00:44:44,070 --> 00:44:44,980
What exactly does it say?

640
00:44:47,760 --> 00:44:48,860
"The Master

641
00:44:49,960 --> 00:44:50,940
is compassionate."

642
00:45:06,260 --> 00:45:09,100
♪Surrounded by chaos, I walk through karmic fire♪

643
00:45:09,300 --> 00:45:12,140
♪And swear this city shall never fall♪

644
00:45:12,380 --> 00:45:15,220
♪The code of honor, the realm's survival♪

645
00:45:15,500 --> 00:45:18,180
♪What must I do to live without shame?♪

646
00:45:18,180 --> 00:45:21,380
♪I fear no fate. My word carries the weight of mountains♪

647
00:45:21,580 --> 00:45:24,420
♪I guard this city, with no retreat, regret, or shame♪

648
00:45:24,740 --> 00:45:27,580
♪One cup of wine settles the storm. I rise like a mountain♪

649
00:45:27,740 --> 00:45:30,580
♪The Mystic Nine stand as one and share the same fate♪

650
00:45:30,700 --> 00:45:31,820
♪Hey♪

651
00:45:32,460 --> 00:45:35,500
♪Who dares mock my defiance?♪

652
00:45:36,780 --> 00:45:42,380
♪No need to pretend or play tricks♪

653
00:45:42,500 --> 00:45:45,580
♪In this one life, I'll brave this thorny road♪

654
00:45:45,700 --> 00:45:48,540
♪With my blood aflame, I'll wrest justice back♪

655
00:45:48,700 --> 00:45:51,140
♪I'll fight my way out of this siege♪

656
00:45:51,700 --> 00:45:54,860
♪And tear the darkness apart♪

657
00:45:54,860 --> 00:45:57,740
♪Pour me a drink, however dark the road ahead♪

658
00:45:57,900 --> 00:46:00,780
♪I'll crush the demons buried deep within♪

659
00:46:01,020 --> 00:46:03,980
♪And let the might of our land resound♪

660
00:46:04,500 --> 00:46:10,660
♪Through life and death, I'll stand with you...♪

661
00:46:23,320 --> 00:46:23,780
Stay back.

662
00:46:25,280 --> 00:46:26,460
Master Zhang has been in a foul mood.

663
00:46:27,230 --> 00:46:28,090
Let him work it off.

664
00:46:29,100 --> 00:46:36,460
♪I believe in neither gods, ghosts, nor reincarnation♪

665
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:39,420
♪In this one life, I'll brave this thorny road♪

666
00:46:39,420 --> 00:46:42,380
♪With my blood aflame, I'll wrest justice back♪

667
00:46:42,540 --> 00:46:44,980
♪I'll fight my way out of this siege♪

668
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:48,740
♪And tear the darkness apart♪

669
00:46:48,740 --> 00:46:51,660
♪Pour me a drink, however dark the road ahead♪

670
00:46:51,660 --> 00:46:54,660
♪I'll crush the demons buried deep within♪

671
00:46:54,900 --> 00:46:57,940
♪And let the might of our land resound♪

672
00:46:58,380 --> 00:47:04,540
♪Through life and death, I'll stand with you♪

673
00:47:16,260 --> 00:47:19,300
♪At the brink, I'll stand with you, with no way back♪

674
00:47:19,540 --> 00:47:22,380
♪I've never regretted defying fate♪

675
00:47:22,540 --> 00:47:25,220
♪I set out, never asking if I'll return♪

676
00:47:25,580 --> 00:47:28,660
♪Even if defeat carves my name in stone♪

677
00:47:28,660 --> 00:47:31,740
♪In this life, we'll break through once more♪

678
00:47:31,740 --> 00:47:34,620
♪Together we'll defend our land and fight our way through♪

679
00:47:34,940 --> 00:47:38,140
♪Stand with me through it all♪

680
00:47:38,340 --> 00:47:47,180
♪Life or death, I'll fight beside you♪

681
00:48:08,480 --> 00:48:09,300
Master Zhang.

682
00:48:19,020 --> 00:48:21,280
[Redeemable for 500 silver coins, Taihe Pleasure House]

683
00:48:21,280 --> 00:48:21,940
Master Zhang,

684
00:48:22,670 --> 00:48:23,780
they work for Ding Qiansui.

685
00:48:24,280 --> 00:48:24,940
I thought so.

686
00:48:31,070 --> 00:48:31,860
Master Zhang,

687
00:48:33,150 --> 00:48:34,210
it hurts terribly.

688
00:48:37,510 --> 00:48:39,260
Last time, you divined that if I treated you harshly,

689
00:48:39,400 --> 00:48:40,380
you'd escape disaster.

690
00:48:40,960 --> 00:48:41,900
Your prediction was right.

691
00:48:43,030 --> 00:48:44,130
Have you escaped it now?

692
00:48:44,230 --> 00:48:45,460
Perhaps not yet.

693
00:49:02,580 --> 00:49:06,740
♪The past fades like smoke♪

694
00:49:07,100 --> 00:49:09,820
♪A choice is made in silence♪

695
00:49:10,100 --> 00:49:12,900
♪In this labyrinthine puzzle♪

696
00:49:13,300 --> 00:49:17,060
♪Who can reach the shore?♪

697
00:49:17,300 --> 00:49:20,740
♪Just an ordinary farewell♪

698
00:49:21,020 --> 00:49:24,420
♪The sun seems to shine bright over our heads♪

699
00:49:24,500 --> 00:49:31,780
♪But this could be our last trip together♪

700
00:49:32,220 --> 00:49:35,500
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

701
00:49:35,780 --> 00:49:39,020
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

702
00:49:39,180 --> 00:49:43,220
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

703
00:49:43,420 --> 00:49:46,780
♪Who believes in fate?♪

704
00:49:47,020 --> 00:49:50,380
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

705
00:49:50,620 --> 00:49:53,900
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

706
00:49:54,220 --> 00:49:57,900
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

707
00:49:58,100 --> 00:50:01,340
♪Take care♪

708
00:50:01,340 --> 00:50:03,900
♪We once raced♪

709
00:50:03,980 --> 00:50:05,900
♪For the dawn♪

710
00:50:06,060 --> 00:50:09,340
♪Ever-lasting bond, a satisfying vindication♪

711
00:50:09,460 --> 00:50:12,740
♪In the web of fate♪

712
00:50:12,740 --> 00:50:15,940
♪No one can escape♪

713
00:50:16,940 --> 00:50:18,780
♪Life and death cut like a blade♪

714
00:50:18,940 --> 00:50:20,500
♪We too were young once♪

715
00:50:20,580 --> 00:50:24,020
♪Fortunate to brave the raging waves together♪

716
00:50:24,220 --> 00:50:26,540
♪Keep the ember lit♪

717
00:50:26,660 --> 00:50:31,180
♪To illuminate the journey ahead♪

718
00:50:31,300 --> 00:50:34,260
♪The spring breeze continues outside♪

719
00:50:34,500 --> 00:50:38,020
♪Who was it who left in such haste?♪

720
00:50:38,140 --> 00:50:41,900
♪Caught in the game, the raging waves fall silent♪

721
00:50:42,220 --> 00:50:45,700
♪Who believes in fate?♪

722
00:50:45,860 --> 00:50:48,860
♪For my home and my country, the years pass like a dream♪

723
00:50:49,100 --> 00:50:52,860
♪When the song ends, who will still be waiting?♪

724
00:50:53,020 --> 00:50:56,740
♪With a nod, we bid farewell and set out again♪

725
00:50:56,860 --> 00:51:08,300
♪Please, do take care of yourself♪
